INSERT OR IGNORE INTO `tournament_match_summaries`
  (`id`,`event_id`,`round`,`best_of`,`leader_one_code`,`archetype_one`,`player_one_name`,`leader_two_code`,`archetype_two`,`player_two_name`,`score_one`,`score_two`,`winner_leader_code`,`winner_side`,`series_complete`,`score_complete`,`summary`,`source_name`,`source_url`,`evidence_status`)
VALUES
  ('london-offline-regional-2026-semifinal-rocks-mihawk','london-offline-regional-2026','Semifinal',3,'OP17-039','Blue Rocks.D.Xebec','Mirco','OP14-020','Green Dracule Mihawk','Davide',1,2,'OP14-020',2,1,1,'Game 1:
Rocks goes second and builds a board and hand with Newgate and Shiki instead of racing. Mihawk develops Laws, then uses 10-cost Shanks and Vander Decken, but does not find the right Luna timing to lock the board. Rocks sticks 10-cost Rocks alongside Newgate and turns its board into repeated 8k–12k attacks. Mihawk runs short on life and counters, and Rocks takes the first game.

Game 2:
Mihawk slows the pace, protects its life, and builds through six-cost Laws and five-cost characters. Rip-Law hand disruption and removal pressure Rocks’ resources while Coffin Boat and Mihawk’s leader ability keep the hand moving. Electrical Luna and a rest event freeze Rocks’ large board for key turns. Mihawk reaches 10 DON, keeps Shanks as a repeat threat, and wins the counter exchange to even the match.

Game 3:
Rocks chooses to go first and pressures with Newgate and repeated leader attacks. Mihawk has a slower curve but rebuilds its hand through the stage, Perona, and Rip-Law. Luna and another rest effect hold Rocks’ developed board while Shanks and Law reduce Rocks’ life. With time running low, Rocks commits to 10-cost Rocks and large attacks but cannot force lethal through Mihawk’s counters. Mihawk converts its remaining board and hand into lethal on the next turn, winning the semifinal 2–1 and advancing to the final against Enel.','User-provided match summary','https://tickets.organizedplay.events/Event/Index/175','VERIFIED');
